// ADR-009 E2 #18 slice 1 — a TYPED `replace module` installs and runs natively
// in both tiers. The comptime `post` handler replaces module `demo`'s body via
// a typed `__ComptimeItemFragment` (`item_fn("answer", "int", 42)`): the
// replacement reaches the directive WITHOUT any source/JSON string, is built
// into a `CheckedModule` (generated provenance stamped, hygienic export symbol
// reserved), and the generated `answer` runs. Printing 42 — not the pre-replace
// 0 — proves the typed replacement shipped. The runtime program is a plain int
// function + a module-qualified call; no async, trait/impl, closure, or
// top-level comptime, so JIT == VM natively (zero [jit-fallback]).
annotation synth_module() {
  targets: [module]
  comptime post(target, ctx) {
    replace module (item_fn("answer", "int", 42))
  }
}

@synth_module()
mod demo {
  fn answer() -> int { 0 }
}

print(demo::answer())
